From 668ff2e35a1d1f9f537b1261f352b43b2ac90436 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunnapatara <kunnapatara@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:31:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(phase-1): correct re-scan messaging, unmeasured luminance
 nullability, and verification semantics

- ComparisonView: eliminate misleading success banner triggered solely by signalsDelta < 0; display verified-resolution messaging only when prior findings are confirmed resolved with evidence; render persisting signals (remainingIssues); display (File comparison unverified) when SHA-256 is missing on either version.
- thumbnailInspector: return meanLuminance as null when measurement fails or cannot be parsed instead of substituting default 128; expose parseLuminanceOutput.
- policyIntelligence: reject resolution when revised domain status is NOT_PROVIDED; compute explicit comparisonStatus on mediaIdentity.
- types: allow meanLuminance to be null in ThumbnailMetadata; add comparisonStatus to mediaIdentity.
- tests: add regression tests for parseLuminanceOutput edge cases, failed luminance extraction, signalsDelta < 0 without verified resolution, skipped and NOT_PROVIDED domains, and SHA-256 comparisonStatus.
